            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This is a reasonable abstraction to help try to clean this up.  I agree, I don't like that the string internals are allowed to \"leak\" here, but it is what it is, at least a method makes it more explicit to where we could potentially change the backing container later."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/message/native_types.hpp",
                    "line": 86,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "If you're going to make change to comments, I'd suggest listing \"direct access to str is deprecated; use string() instead\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/message/native_types.hpp",
                    "line": 86,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "applied."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/message/native_types.hpp",
                    "line": 160,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "In your commit message you state that using `object_path::str` is an anti-pattern and that `string()` should be used instead (as also mentioned in the comment you've added to `std::string str`.) But at the same time, the comment added directly on `string()` itself then says:\n> avoid using this function for new code if 'filename()' / 'parent_path()' / ... will do.\n\nThis is, in my opinion, confusing as they point in opposite directions. One says \"prefer `string()`\", the other says \"avoid `string()`\". It'd help to clarify the intended hierarchy of preference here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/message/native_types.hpp",
                    "line": 160,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "The comments are indirection among each other.\n\nThe API user (instead of being left guessing) is directed to the preferred API.\n\nThe order of preference is (from most to least preferred):\n- `object_path::filename()` | `object_path::parent_path()` | ...\n- `object_path::string()`\n- direct `object_path::str` reading the internal value\n- direct `object_path::str` access, changing the internal value in some way\n\nThe problem is that it really depends on the use-case and the amount of refactoring someone is willing to do which one they will use.\n\nThere is no single direct replacement for `object_path::string()` i could point to, right?\n\nI'm very much open to change the comments if you would like to suggest a change (gerrit has a feature to directly suggest an edit)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/message/native_types.hpp",
                    "line": 160,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I would almost advocate for wording the comment stronger here.\n\n\"This should not be used in new code.  Use filename() or parent_path() appropriately\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/sdbusplus/message/native_types.hpp",
                    "line": 160,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> I would almost advocate for wording the comment stronger here.\n\napplied."
                }
            ],
